            <title xml:id="title_c7b92025" xml:lang="da">Rebus</title>
            <title xml:id="title_bc435c48" xml:lang="de">Drei kleine Clavierstücke</title>
            <title xml:id="title_c036103f" xml:lang="en">Three Little Piano Pieces</title>
            <title type="subordinate" xml:id="title_f31ca993" xml:lang="da">Claveerstykker</title>
            <contributor xml:id="respStmt_83be041d">
               <persName role="composer" xml:id="persName_id6617e35a">Niels W. Gade</persName>
               <persName role="dedicatee" xml:id="persName_0b29f471">Oluf Bachlin</persName>
            </contributor>
            <creation xml:id="creation_id704dfc2b">
               <date isodate="1875" xml:id="date_8ffa7f11">1875</date>
               <geogName xml:id="geogName_idb2a52800"/>
            </creation>
            <history xml:id="history_id52561d94">
               <p xml:id="idm288">In Denmark the three pieces were published without opus number under the title "Rebus". The title refers to the fact that all three pices are based on combinations of the notes B - A - C - H and G - A - D - E.  In Germany they were published under the title "Drei kleine Klavierstücke" with the opus number 2 dedicated to Oluf Bachlin, which is probably a constructed name. However, the opus number 2 had already been used by the German publishing firm F.W. Arnold in Dresden for Gade's "Frühlingsblumen". Therefore Carl Gurckhaus of the firm Fr. Kistner asked Gade to choose another number, but for unknown reasons he insisted on keeping this opus number, which might lead to the wrong conclusion that it is a juvenile work.</p>
            </history>
